{
  "about": "Which on-screen labels in the docs open a place in MAYA. The docs linker (app-linker.mjs) turns every <Ui> whose words are listed here, and every listed phrase in plain text, into a link that only signed-in readers see. Only places are listed (tabs, pages, sections, panels, columns, banners, and buttons whose job is to open one). Form fields and actions are never linked: a link must never look like it saves or sends. Page overrides win; null means leave it as words there. A key ending in /* covers every page in that section. A phrase starting with \"the \" needs the article to match but links only the words after it; a phrase set to null is never linked and shields a longer phrase (\"the calendar date\") from a shorter one. A label that names two places (\"Conditions\" is a column of the rules list and a section of the rule builder) is listed for the commoner one, and the page sets the other by hand: <Ui to=\"rules.new\" q=\"focus=conditions\">.",
